  "comment": "The blocks of the signal chain as both UIs show them (docs/design/APP_PLAN.md 3.5): order, names, colours, and which settings belong to each. Settings are named by their serial key (lib/params ParamDefs.cpp); '@Name' names a setting that has no key. 'on' is the block's switch; 'onInverted' means the setting is a bypass. 'file' is the loaded file the block shows: 'model' or 'ir'. 'summary' is the setting whose value the block's tile shows. 'peak' is the block's place among the METERS frame's block peaks (its output level). 'activity' is the METERS bit that shows the block is working. 'master' is the unit's master volume, the last gain before the DAC: one value for all presets, kept in the unit's own settings and not in presets, so it is shown apart from the blocks, beside the meters. The cab block holds the two gains that act right after the cab: the output gain (global) and the preset's level. A setting no block names is shown under 'Other', so nothing can go missing.",
